<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Garage packages in Calgary are fixed-spec detached garages that a builder sells at a published starting price: a slab, framing, siding, shingles, an overhead door and a basic electrical subpanel in a set size. Sizes run from a single around 14 x 20 through the 20 x 20, 22 x 22 and 24 x 24 doubles up to a triple. Back Lane Garage Co is advertising, not a builder. The independent garage builder who quotes your job signs the contract with you and applies for the permits.</p><p>The advertised price is only the start of a comparison. Two packages a few thousand dollars apart on the page can differ in wall height, electrical capacity, door size, and whether permits and GST are in the number. This page shows what Calgary builders publish, what 'starting from' tends to leave out, and how to line two packages up row by row. To get two or three comparable written quotes, call <strong>(403) 555-0162</strong>.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Fixed sizes, named prices</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Venkor Group, Corsac Construction and Calgary Garage Builders Ltd each publish set sizes and starting prices. Every figure on this page is attributed to the firm that advertises it.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Read the inclusions, not the headline</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Published packages typically cover a slab, stud framing, vinyl siding, shingles, an overhead door and a subpanel. Wall height, door size and amperage differ from firm to firm.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">A list of what 'starting from' leaves out</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Upgrades, site prep, demolition of an old garage, electrical capacity, heat and GST are where a starting price drifts. Published figures are attached wherever they exist.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Permits kept separate</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The City of Calgary lists a 2026 building permit fee of $333.84 for a new garage. Some builders fold permits into the package and some do not, so the quote has to say.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">A line-by-line comparison method</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Footprint, wall height, slab, door, electrical, permits, GST and payment terms go on one sheet. Two quotes are comparable only when every row matches.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Where a package stops fitting</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Slabs over 592 sq ft, walls over 3 m to the truss and oversized doors push a job off the standard package. You get the thresholds, so you know before you ask.</p>
      </div>
</div>
